    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarsus</span></b> , i, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the capital of
			Cilicia</i>, now <i>Tersoos</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				2, 17, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 5, 20, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			225</span></i>; Auct. B. Alex. 66. — Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarsensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tarsus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelagus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
					16</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.— Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarsenses</span></b> , ium, m.,
				<i>the inhabitants of Tarsus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				12, 13, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 5, 21, 7</span></i>.</div>
